 @Shadowninja1200  lol, those lists just analyzes western releases and AAA titles, and it's a wiki page based on people like you and me to add games to that list, so by any stretch it is extremely incomplete. I can't even find many of the online games I've played like Cabal, Chaos Online, FireFall, Tera, GuildWars2, ESO, PoE, DragonNest...

Also yes, TV's are a different story because the watchable screen is, well let's just say generally above 32 inches... But we're talking about gaming here and most PC users has a monitor that fits on a desk, there's also a difference in filming pictures in 4K for TV and making textures from scratch in 4K for games, wouldn't you agree? I can pick up my phone and shoot a 4K video in a second, but drawing a texture in 4K detail would take me a long while, and the same applies to game developers... It's too expensive and thus most just scales the textures and scaled textures are not native 4K textures... Don't be fooled just because it's branded 4K.

"4K" to me means not just resolution, I could scale HalfLife up to 16K resolution but it wouldn't look any better because the textures aren't designed for 4K, do you catch my drift here? The market works like this, and the same applies to DX12, they just port the game from DX11 to DX12 and put a DX12 sticker on it... Same applies to 4K, just because they add the resolution to your options doesn't mean it's native 4K.

