 @rijujakhar8771  Basically, a forwarding service is a warehouse that you pay for so you could have the items that you buy in another country shipped to them in that same country, then they will ship it directly to you.

For example, if you wanna buy something from US, they will give you a US address which you could then use to send anything you want to. Be careful though, it's only cheaper in certain cases so make sure to calculate your expenditures with the cheapest forwarding service in your country to see if it's worth it.

For me so far, everything I've bought through forwarding has cost me 2x less than what I would pay for locally. And haven't had any problems with broken/missing stuff.

 @robertjif6337  Eh, reveal showcases are ALWAYS going to show the best possible case, and the games that they worked hardest on optimizing. Things to consider:

-The games they showed were probably the games that had the highest increased performance, but that doesn't make the increase meaningless. The 3080 really is a beefy card especially at the price point, and even if it's only a 15-20% increase for some games,  that's still huge.

-Point 2, and honestly this is the most important point, this card isn't out yet. The 2080Ti has had two years of driver updates and game optimizations. The 3080 will only get stronger on these current games, it's even not unheard of for Nvidia to release a driver that gets an extra 5-10% performance for popular games that drops weeks or months after card release. So if it's ALREADY this much better, I'm pretty optimistic about the future. It's a good time to be a gamer.

